    "body": "## Summary\nThe MXFP8 THD test helper passes flat capacity buffers to a binder that requires `(T, H, D)` or `(B, H, S, D)` operand geometry, causing rejection before kernel execution.\n\n## Fix\nBind zero-copy `(capacity_tokens, heads, head_dim)` views for Q, K, V, and O. This preserves each allocation and its NaN-poisoned capacity tail, while keeping the existing numerical references and auxiliary tensors unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n- Python syntax and whitespace checks pass.\n- Real CPU PyTorch 2.14.1 checks pass in 60 scenarios (240 operand views): FP8 inputs, multiple output dtypes, empty capacities, grouped heads, differing V dimensions, preserved storage aliases, output-write propagation, and NaN capacity tails. The original flat representation is rejected by the current Python geometry predicate.\n\n## Manual verification\n\n[SUPERSEDED] Continued in https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend/pull/1720 with a descriptive source branch. GPU/native-binder validation remains incomplete.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
